# Large binaries - never commit
*.bin
*.img
*.dat
*.br
*.elf
*.gz

# OTA and extraction artifacts
7.3.1.9/
ota-extract/
ota-*/

# Reference clones (documented in docs/references.md, re-clone as needed)
refs/

# Device dumps. Partition images may contain serials and unique data, so they are
# never committed -- but the *documentation* around them must be, otherwise a
# clone has no way to regenerate or verify a dump. The negations below are
# required: without them a bare `git add -A` silently skips these three files.
dumps/*
!dumps/README.md
!dumps/SHA256SUMS.txt
!dumps/dump-small.sh
diagnostics/*.gz
diagnostics/config

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

diagnostics/stage0-report.json

OTAs/

stage1-root/prebuilt-ps7319/

*.upstream.bak

# Reddit-guide MTK toolchain (third-party binaries, analyzed in stage2-unlock/README.md)
stage2-unlock/mediatekTools/

# Handoff bundle and its export.
#
# stage2a-unlock/ is a DISTRIBUTION SNAPSHOT: every file in it is a copy of a
# tracked file (plus its own reviewer-facing README.md). Tracking the copies is
# what made the bundle go stale twice -- an edit to the repo did not touch the
# bundle, and the bundle was then zipped and shipped anyway.
#
# It is now generated on demand instead:
#     python tools/sync-handoff-bundle.py     # copy from repo + rewrite MANIFEST.txt
#     python tools/check-bundle-drift.py      # prove the bundle matches the repo
#     & 'C:\Program Files\7-Zip\7z.exe' a -tzip -mx=9 stage2a-unlock<date>.zip stage2a-unlock
#
# Both the directory and the export stay out of git; the tracked source of truth
# is the repo itself.
stage2a-unlock/
stage2a-unlock*.zip

# Stage 4 builds the actor APK from app/ source, so the output is generated, not
# source. `sh stage4-persistent/app/build.sh` recreates it; committing it would
# mean shipping a binary that can silently drift from the source preflight checks.
stage4-persistent/app/build/

# Private optimization inventories, plans, measurements and rollback journals.
stage5-optimize/runs/
# Frontier-model repository assessments. These are external critiques kept for
# reference; they are not part of the repo's own claims and must not be published
# (they quote private paths and internal reasoning). Kept out of git and out of
# the public export deliberately.
docs/repository-assessment.md
docs/*assessment*.md

# Stage 1's staging marker. This records what was staged on THIS machine, for
# THIS device and build -- it is local state, not repository content. It was
# tracked once, which meant a fresh clone already had it and skipped the staging
# that makes the chain work. root_poc.sh now writes a content-keyed marker and
# only skips staging when device, build and carrier hash all still match.
stage1-root/port/.assets-staged.*.sha256
